# DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF RULES, and the emptiness is the mechanism.
#
# This file used to carry fifty-two rules, and between them they hid 343 MB of
# output inside a 4 MB source repository: generated harnesses beside their
# generators, subjects beside the bundlers that wrote them, blobs, emitted zig,
# and 177 bare-metal truths kept by an explicit `!truth/**/*.truth` exception.
# Nothing ever cleaned any of it because nothing ever SAW it -- `git status` was
# clean the whole time it accumulated.
#
# Steve, 2026-09-04: "nuke every item from gitignore, which is the root of all
# evil ... we want git status to LOUDLY TELL US when we're polluting the repo
# checkout."
#
# So there are no rules. Every generated file a script writes into this checkout
# turns up as untracked, immediately, in every `git status` anybody runs. The fix
# for a noisy status is to make the script write into the SANDBOX -- never to add
# a line here.
#
# If you are about to add a rule, you are about to hide something.
